-- l4 explore keys a state on the answer a zero-input rule that reads a
-- ledger was forced to, because the evaluator keeps a rule's first answer.
-- `go peek` forces `taken now` to FALSE before `taken` is committed, and
-- `go skip` does not, so after `go peek` Bob may buy again (the kept FALSE)
-- and after `go skip` he may not (forced now, TRUE): two states. This file
-- calls the ledger reader positionally; named.l4, genitive.l4 and wrapper.l4
-- spell the same call with WITH, as a genitive, and through a wrapper, and
-- each must explore to the same graph (smucclaw/l4-ide#1107, after review:
-- on unstable they merged the two states into one).

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVEN dflt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is taken` dflt MEANS fromMaybe dflt (RECALL OFFICIAL's `taken`)

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`taken now` MEANS `is taken` FALSE

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
